fact WorkItem(id: "WI-288", description: some(value: "Scala loader/typer: consume WI-185/WI-269 parser hints (type_name, type_args, type_params)\n\nFollow-up to the parser-only Phase A port (effectSet tightening WI-092, let type annotation WI-185, operation type params WI-269). The Scala parser now emits IR the loader/typer ignores:\n\n1. loadLetExpr (Loader.scala ~633) reads only posArgs and drops the 'type_name' named-arg, so the WI-185 let type annotation never reaches the typer. Read fn.namedArgs and thread the hint through.\n\n2. loadApplyOrConstructor (Loader.scala ~705) treats the injected 'type_args' named-arg as an ordinary call argument, so Name[bindings](args) loads with a spurious value argument instead of as type arguments. Recognize/strip 'type_args' and route it as call-site type bindings.\n\n3. typeExprToRef (AnthillParser.scala ~352) has no case for TypeExpr.Arrow / TupleType and falls through to a Ref(\"_\") sentinel; arrow/tuple annotations and positional bindings silently degrade. Extend coverage.\n\n4. Operation.typeParams is parsed and stored but not consumed by the Scala loader/typer (rust consumes it in kb/load.rs + kb/typing.rs). Wire it in to close the dual-typer gap.\n\nRust is ground truth here; these are the Scala-side catch-up items."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "scaland-sbt-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-05-23T09:18:45Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-288", author: "user", content: "Rescoped to the substrate-neutral fix. Investigation found the WI's premise was partly off: items 1,2,4 target a Scala loader/typer that does not exist yet — convertExprTerm + load* helpers are DEAD CODE (no caller), operations are never loaded into the KB as OperationInfo facts, and there is no native-Scala typer. Those three items only become meaningful/testable once operation-body loading exists, and the loader's term-building is itself in the path of the in-flight Term->Value resolver migration (rustland WI-246). Delivered here: item 3 — typeExprToRef (AnthillParser.scala) now lowers TypeExpr.Arrow -> anthill.prelude.Type.arrow(effects,param,result) and TypeExpr.TupleType/multi-param-arrow -> Type.named_tuple(fields: List[TypeField]), mirroring rustland type_expr_to_term, replacing the silent Ref(\"_\") sentinel. This is purely parser-side (upstream of the resolver), substrate-neutral, and tested (3 new ParseTest cases; full scaland suite 145 green). Items 1,2,4 + operation-body loading + typer seeding moved to WI-294 (depends on WI-288), gated behind the scaland Value migration.", at: "2026-05-23T09:18:40Z")
